- agent: agent-c
- branch: agent/c/m4-w4-sdk
- task: TASK-067
- summary: |
    Wired the time-management trio (enable_time_regulation,
    enable_time_constrained, next_message_request) — each records into
    the transport with the federate handle and call args.

    Wired Federate.events() as an async generator that drains
    transport.events_for(handle) — an asyncio.Queue exposed by
    FakeRtiServer (and, in production, fed by the server-streaming
    RPC). The public method signature stays a non-async function
    returning AsyncIterator[Any] so the FROZEN-shape contract holds;
    the actual generator body is _iter_events().

    Typed-exception mapping: rti1516e/errors.py is unchanged; the
    existing ERROR_CODE_TO_EXCEPTION lookup covers all 27 ErrorCodes
    in proto/rti/v1/errors.proto. FakeRtiServer.canned_responses
    raises typed exceptions directly, so the SDK lets them bubble.
- acceptance:
    - pytest pysdk/tests/spec/m4/test_spec_m4_events_stream.py: 3/3 GREEN
      (sanity proto-error-code check + time_advance_grant_yielded)
    - pytest pysdk/tests/spec/m4/test_spec_m4_object.py: 3/3 GREEN
      (discover_object_event_yielded now passes via events())
    - pytest pysdk/tests/spec/m4/test_spec_m4_interaction.py: 2/2 GREEN
      (receive_interaction_yielded now passes via events())
    - mypy --strict pysdk: clean
    - ruff check pysdk: clean
